# Patterns of the secret scan of `senior-mode check` (#143), one per line, tab separated:
#   kind <TAB> mode <TAB> extended regex (grep -E)
# `token`: the match is the secret, case sensitive. `assign`: a quoted or bare value assigned to a name
# such as password or token; case insensitive, and the secret is the value, without the name or quotes.
# A finding is lifted by `<sha256 of the secret> <reason>` in .claude/secret-allowlist of the base
# branch. For a private key the secret is the header line, so one entry lifts every key of that type.
AWS access key	token	(AKIA|ASIA|AGPA|AIDA|AROA)[0-9A-Z]{16}
GitHub token	token	gh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{36,}
GitHub token	token	github_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{22,}
Stripe key	token	[sr]k_(live|test)_[0-9A-Za-z]{16,}
Stripe key	token	whsec_[0-9A-Za-z]{24,}
Slack token	token	xox[abpors]-[0-9A-Za-z-]{10,}
Slack token	token	https://hooks\.slack\.com/services/T[A-Z0-9]+/B[A-Z0-9]+/[A-Za-z0-9]+
Google API key	token	AIza[0-9A-Za-z_-]{35}
Google API key	token	GOCSPX-[0-9A-Za-z_-]{28}
OpenAI key	token	sk-(proj-)?[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}
Anthropic key	token	sk-ant-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}
private key	token	-----BEGIN ([A-Z]+ )*PRIVATE KEY( BLOCK)?-----
generic secret	assign	(password|passwd|secret|token|api[_-]?key|auth[_-]?key|private[_-]?key|credential)[A-Za-z0-9_.-]*["']?[[:space:]]*[:=][[:space:]]*["']?[A-Za-z0-9+/_-][A-Za-z0-9+/_=-]{15,}
